            <ArticleTitle>[Laparoscopic hemi-hysterectomy for pseudo unicornuate uterus: apropos of 3 cases].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>793-796</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Surgical management of unicornuate uterus with rudimentary horn is justified because of disabling dysmenorrhea but also because of associated morbidity and mortality complications. We describe here three new cases of laparoscopic removal of the horn following a new improved surgical technique.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
